{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_21bcf4ec6d99827d6cc427fcbe821fefc06ff85f931d7ca018065f7ca40a9173","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"gsa-tts/agentic-coding-quickstart@e0b9a3b60d87 snapshot 1c3580d2ef2330cc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0e9a6905a48fd0e0a320603755b2d2d5753e7dbd04ee8b80708e04855dbe84ea"],"source_ids":["src_f7af68416c0c53beb65224294d6d7d69"],"text":"msb cannot mount symlinked host paths (failing with 'Not a directory'), so acq canonicalizes workspaces; macOS $TMPDIR paths under /var fail unless resolved to /private/var.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3cced06c7f668f2b0f0390a590ce4801bd68a187f4ad2e5dc57de66f03774dc1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"gsa-tts/agentic-coding-quickstart@e0b9a3b60d87 snapshot 1c3580d2ef2330cc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3264ab646df7e3bd8333db87c64687bed0bd7239ea6e729923be12f1cd3ecdbb","slc_6c1bfc0e142271f2f8fcbbbd57fc2c812028571b023f094488f8197aa382cec7","slc_71dd1a5a1d3963a878bc28e83cae854b3fad8d7294edc2d308e1a7438a97abc6","slc_92460622b23b90c2a3a4fea6aeaa924d39d98841dc3a23c3457cdb86c0385df5","slc_a131aa5140bc45358aa3eb6b11b5c33458f19af2f8c37eece2b49737377d51ee","slc_fed7192dff53728916154373895367393476757f7be079ce12108e858752e235"],"source_ids":["src_f7af68416c0c53beb65224294d6d7d69"],"text":"Backend selection is exposed via `acq backend set <name>`, a per-invocation `--backend` flag, and the `ACQ_BACKEND` environment variable.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_48943dbfaf9facae9d6e09e77b8c14547c34dddc49d9c1ff44dad1ca2ba20608","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"gsa-tts/agentic-coding-quickstart@e0b9a3b60d87 snapshot 1c3580d2ef2330cc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0676e45d317af70254b66847b95099a4e71ce496340cc86f0906e44e8b59c4c8","slc_93dcd63f32e2a036194828ed4b907b3ec80308b110d3be1a6cdd6a4e8085ee5b","slc_a6c79992a01487163a1e98bfc52357490a2562b4b3d2e74afd88259b1656644e"],"source_ids":["src_ca5d5fff1b9b51e286b58280ed68180d"],"text":"The product's entry point is the `acq` CLI, invoked e.g. as `acq run opencode ~/my-project`, which runs the agent in a sandbox configured for federal usage.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_632bea2423d1c83f8de31755260d4da72e9db51225a57dec581c0e1e7ac23330","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"gsa-tts/agentic-coding-quickstart@e0b9a3b60d87 snapshot 1c3580d2ef2330cc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_19a592359bfb07715a0672e790f47075e9044d0ec61664401ec483b8857c6245","slc_87f2a247edb22a2441924b86b8f22252945411a9c0302650349b9cf2adb18b69","slc_d80e0b3b524545f1e14b943c532234d7c064b90d793c5f8808efd3cec1f61185"],"source_ids":["src_f7af68416c0c53beb65224294d6d7d69"],"text":"A backend-neutral custom base image can be set with `--image` or `ACQ_IMAGE`; precedence is flag > env > backend-specific variable, and an explicitly set `ACQ_MSB_IMAGE` wins over the neutral knob with a notice.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6722ca9a4503e8da86de84d6c4fb2cb0f3f50c9690a92fca3f352b422c374fdc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"gsa-tts/agentic-coding-quickstart@e0b9a3b60d87 snapshot 1c3580d2ef2330cc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_83536b64123f99a120c0ebe2738fb1fae10d0c4a4f630bb2a0edade156c324a8","slc_84c748d5eaafa0a19ad05fdd7bfeffe65f4ea4d4afb0c2358a3f1ba3801536e4"],"source_ids":["src_f7af68416c0c53beb65224294d6d7d69"],"text":"Although microsandbox has a snapshot CLI, acq does not surface it, so `ACQ_BACKEND_SUPPORTS_SNAPSHOTS=0` reflects what acq exposes rather than msb's capability.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6a20a6de2f79815591eb74c0197bc0ed37078855cf33ec492ab6fa37bcd9382e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"gsa-tts/agentic-coding-quickstart@e0b9a3b60d87 snapshot 1c3580d2ef2330cc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9281612798caf00139d77531d196ac2399543e56c395e7a0c713ab3bd58ba496","slc_b6a65ac25d441bf2c95fd4596f2dd35e965123a645aac6482454cc2a72267814"],"source_ids":["src_f7af68416c0c53beb65224294d6d7d69"],"text":"The sbx backend requires the sbx CLI >= 0.38.0 (for the v2 kit grammar) plus a Docker account, while the msb backend requires msb >= 0.6.8 and host virtualization (KVM, Apple Silicon HVF, or Windows WHP).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_716833d4b1537dab00f86cfb1764f13d54581aed86f384bc781595fc1b9a8727","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"gsa-tts/agentic-coding-quickstart@e0b9a3b60d87 snapshot 1c3580d2ef2330cc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9316d4ce201bd969990a51b07bf142e1d29a3fcf626c0dcfba2763d1e07b5830","slc_a6c79992a01487163a1e98bfc52357490a2562b4b3d2e74afd88259b1656644e","slc_b07224613189df894d116c729140fcb21e1a26f5a94ce541d434ed392d7133f8"],"source_ids":["src_ca5d5fff1b9b51e286b58280ed68180d","src_f7af68416c0c53beb65224294d6d7d69"],"text":"acq supports two shipped isolation backends: msb (microsandbox, a lightweight open-source microVM runtime, the default) and sbx (Docker Sandboxes), with a Podman-based 'ppp' backend listed as in development.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7e0680100f3993f23071f16f3890eab718e31ca70b9dc01015d27ff26813b1b0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"gsa-tts/agentic-coding-quickstart@e0b9a3b60d87 snapshot 1c3580d2ef2330cc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_87b80028c9069a3e546a01ab7d56d29dae40cc63d6fcfe357aa05c7ab21446ea","slc_c8e415c9d8845ceb40b2b7612f4170b69df85c080886f1336af820ef18eb2272"],"source_ids":["src_f7af68416c0c53beb65224294d6d7d69"],"text":"On sbx 0.38, `sbx kit add` cannot apply startup-bearing kits to a live sandbox, so the built-in kit bundle can only be extended by recreating the sandbox; msb is unaffected.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a4600bd06623848c727681178028fff7c21b85aef18643951c0cd1620d0e77eb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"gsa-tts/agentic-coding-quickstart@e0b9a3b60d87 snapshot 1c3580d2ef2330cc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1c853f5a8293c50bad87fb8bcb8cba8f41b725f93dc414de5eae84f909d7526a","slc_adb4e7d1c1de9456df7f848bcbc5bd4e2702f0d6bfd95278b03d23729e0d814d"],"source_ids":["src_ca5d5fff1b9b51e286b58280ed68180d"],"text":"The quickstart targets federal teams using AI coding agents, connecting them to USAi (GSA's LLM gateway at api.gsa.usai.gov), and is classified as a local development environment for Low/Moderate-impact work, not a production/hosted environment.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d0ba634522f37ab024d8e9e5d7d8dc6b73299a4817392db6862c88ffdc5bf36c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"gsa-tts/agentic-coding-quickstart@e0b9a3b60d87 snapshot 1c3580d2ef2330cc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1e0bf47ba9754a29313bde1f0e860055df0887fe378b5a716b91fbd28d79827d","slc_26bc367b7fb540e7e88564159126acf674d0b836a638f8ed2a7e9c8ce13f7bd9","slc_83536b64123f99a120c0ebe2738fb1fae10d0c4a4f630bb2a0edade156c324a8","slc_c8e415c9d8845ceb40b2b7612f4170b69df85c080886f1336af820ef18eb2272"],"source_ids":["src_ca5d5fff1b9b51e286b58280ed68180d","src_f7af68416c0c53beb65224294d6d7d69"],"text":"Secrets are injected at runtime via a proxy/host-env binding (e.g. `--secret USAI_API_KEY@api.gsa.usai.gov`), so real secret values never enter the guest VM or container.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d58b51a625f9387cadaee2583fe719821051e98f6e17166bf76b499279253cf7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"gsa-tts/agentic-coding-quickstart@e0b9a3b60d87 snapshot 1c3580d2ef2330cc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8736d528d91b67be2a79ddb81a129aeb8b93cbb4dd2cceb1f27780140906bd2c","slc_d4aee5c3417d603d61dbebda725ce1b3d6ee19fa4c045706eb2e233af9e47f54","slc_ebeb74c837735220a4b0f6a16f67b431de3bdfea4fb9d64fd88a7b44602853cb"],"source_ids":["src_f7af68416c0c53beb65224294d6d7d69"],"text":"Network egress is selected by a backend-neutral tier variable `ACQ_NETWORK_TIER` (strict, balanced, open; default balanced); strict and balanced are deny-by-default with allowlists, and `open` requires an explicit confirmation variable.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_eaefae11f3ee353787874776163f43a32a7ef20b75c67b93c73163277bb12d99","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"gsa-tts/agentic-coding-quickstart@e0b9a3b60d87 snapshot 1c3580d2ef2330cc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_802434f19cbe699974e0fb833e901571fe21f96537950c1056d324d1c595350d","slc_809543d0c087430aa006a4b3bf1590d75f3ede47a8f7c42098715775f1025024"],"source_ids":["src_ca5d5fff1b9b51e286b58280ed68180d"],"text":"The companion playbook provides agent skills following the agentskills.io standard (e.g. federal-security-controls-lookup, ato-package, code-review), symlinked into ~/.agents/skills when a sandbox launches so agents discover them automatically.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ec67fd4b090e8fa5fbcf3e8e84a541fd305328395e2b4e7bc51572c2050a0fad","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"gsa-tts/agentic-coding-quickstart@e0b9a3b60d87 snapshot 1c3580d2ef2330cc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_935c8cb034bdca04030680c9062670dbe780ddb9871c9a6df8c868cb650b0585"],"source_ids":["src_f7af68416c0c53beb65224294d6d7d69"],"text":"The msb backend defaults sandboxes to 4 GiB RAM and 2 vCPUs (overriding msb's 512 MiB/1 vCPU, which OOM-kills Node TUI agents), tunable via ACQ_MSB_MEMORY/ACQ_MSB_CPUS.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6a21912604ea489d8042fb77e9eae7f3"}
